#: tips.cc:3
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can synchronize your calendar data with the data on a Palm "
"Pilot by using <a "
"href=\"http://www.slac.com/pilone/kpilot_home\">KPilot</a>?\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...y gallwch gydamseru eich data calendr efo'r data ar Palm Pilot\n"
" gan ddefnyddio <a "
"href=\"http://www.slac.com/pilone/kpilot_home\">KPilot</a>?\n"

#: tips.cc:7
msgid ""
"<p>...that it is possible to show the current time in the calendar? Enable "
"the Marcus Bains line in the dialog which appears after selecting "
"<b>Settings</b>,\n"
"<b>KOrganizer settings...</b> from the menu bar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:12
msgid ""
"<p>...that KOrganizer supports Microsoft Exchange? Just enable the plugin "
"<b>Microsoft® Exchange 2000 plugin for KOrganizer</b> in the dialog "
"<b>Configure Plugins...</b> from the <b>Settings</b> menu.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:16
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can select whether the week starts on Monday or on Sunday in "
"the KDE Control Center? KOrganizer uses this setting. Look at Regional & "
"Accessibility->Country/Region & Languages, then select the Time & Dates "
"tab.\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...y gallwch ddewis a ddylai'r wythnos ddechrau ar ddydd Llun neu ddydd "
"Sul yn y Ganolfan Reoli KDE?\n"
" Mae kTrefnydd yn defnyddio'r gosodiad yma.  Ewch i Personoleiddio -> Gwlad "
"&\n"
" Ieithoedd, ar y Tab Amser & Dyddiadau.\n"

#: tips.cc:20
msgid ""
"<p>"
"...that you can edit to-dos quickly by right clicking on the property you "
"wish to change; like the priority, the category or the date?\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:24
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can view and edit a calendar from the shell with "
"konsolekalendar? Run <b>konsolekalendar --help</b> for the available "
"options.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:28
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can import birthdays from your address book? There is a "
"resource available which connects the birthdays to your calendar; it is even "
"possible to set a reminder for each event.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:32
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can store your calendar on an FTP server? Use the standard "
"file dialog to save the calendar to a URL like "
"<b>ftp://username@ftpserver/filename</b>. You can make your calendar active "
"and load and save it as if it were local. Just make sure that no two "
"KOrganizer applications are working on the same file, at the same time.\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...y gallwch storio eich calendr ar weinydd FTP? Defnyddiwch yr ymgom\n"
" ffeil safonol i gadw'r calendr i  URL fel  "
"<b>ftp://enw-defnyddiwr@gweinydd-ftp/enw-ffeil</b>.\n"
" Gallwch wneud eich calendr yn weithredol, a'i llwytho a'i gadw, fel petae "
"yn leol.\n"
" Ond sicrhewch nad ydy dau gymhwysiant KTrefnydd yn gweithio ar yr un ffeil\n"
" wrth yr un amser.\n"

#: tips.cc:36
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can create hierarchical to-dos by clicking with the right "
"mouse button on an existing to-do and selecting <b>New Sub-to-do</b> from "
"the context menu?\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...y gallwch greu I'w-Wneudau hierarchaidd gan glicio efo\n"
" botwm dde'r lygoden ar I'w-Wneud sy'n bodoli a dewis <b>Is-I'w-Wneud "
"Newydd</b> oddiar y ddewislen cyd-destun?\n"

#: tips.cc:40
msgid ""
"<p>...that a color can be assigned to each category? Events with a certain "
"category will be shown in that color. You can assign these in the section "
"<b>Colors</b> within the dialog which appears after selecting "
"<b>Settings</b>, <b>KOrganizer settings...</b> from the menu bar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:44
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can view and edit a calendar with Konqueror? Just click on "
"the calendar file to make Konqueror open it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:48
msgid ""
"<p>...that it is possible to add an attachment to an event? To do so, add a "
"link to the <b>Attachments</b> tab within the <b>Edit Event</b> dialog.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:52
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can export your calendar to HTML? Check the plugin <b>Web "
"export plugin for KOrganizer</b> in the dialog <b>Configure Plugins...</b> "
"from the <b>Settings</b> menu. Now you can export your calendar with "
"<b>File</b>, <b>Export</b>, <b>Export Web Page...</b> from the menu bar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:56
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can purge completed to-dos in one step? Go to the <b>File</b>"
" menu and choose <b>Purge Completed</b>.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:60
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can create a new sub-to-do by pasting a to-do while another "
"one is selected?\n"
msgstr ""

